<h1>fudic_contract</h1>

<p><code>fudic_contract</code> lista cada declaración de un <code>.fudapi</code> que necesita un handler: su firma en TypeScript, el fichero en el que va y si está escrito. Para lo que falta, responde un esqueleto que compila. Lo cuenta <a href="/docs/server">Servidor</a>.</p>

<h2 id="arguments">Argumentos</h2>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr><th scope="col">Argumento</th><th scope="col">Tipo</th><th scope="col">Qué es</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><td><code>id</code></td><td>texto</td><td>El id del <code>.fudapi</code>: su ruta bajo <code>src/</code>, sin la extensión (<code>routes/products</code>).</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="example">Ejemplo</h2>

<p>Con la función <code>search</code> recién declarada y sin handler:</p>

<ui-code>
<pre><code>fudic_contract &#123; "id": "routes/products" &#125;</code></pre>
</ui-code>

<ui-code>
<pre><code>&#123;
  "id": "routes/products",
  "handlers": [
    &#123;
      "name": "routes/products.load",
      "exported": "load",
      "state": "connected",
      "file": "src/server/routes/products.ts",
      "signature": "/** The data of the page, read on the server: its handler is in src/server/routes/products.ts. */\nexport interface …",
      "implementedIn": [
        "src/server/routes/products.ts"
      ]
    &#125;,
    &#123;
      "name": "routes/products.search",
      "exported": "search",
      "state": "missing",
      "file": "src/server/routes/products.ts",
      "signature": "/** The products whose name contains q. */\nexport type SearchCtx = FnContext&lt;&#123;&#125;, &#123;&#125;, &#123; readonly q: string &#125;&gt;;\nexport …",
      "implementedIn": []
    &#125;
  ],
  "skeleton": [
    &#123;
      "file": "src/server/routes/products.ts",
      "exists": true,
      "text": "import &#123; search &#125; from 'fudic:routes/products';\n\nsearch.handle(() =&gt; &#123;\n  throw new Error('routes/products.search: not written yet');\n&#125;);\n"
    &#125;
  ],
  "diagnostics": [],
  "next": "Write the skeleton in src/server/routes/products.ts (add to a file that exists), then replace each throw with the real …"
&#125;</code></pre>
</ui-code>

